ook out for the  safety of children several states and  cities have taken action to educate  enforce and strengthen the laws  surrounding school buses police in  Westland Michigan conducted this sting  operation in 2016 stopping several  drivers who blew past a stopped school  bus and posting this video to Facebook  as a warning lawmakers in Mississippi  went a step further after five year old  Nathan ki was killed in 2009 the state  passed  Nathan's law in 2011 which increased  fines for illegally passing stopped  school buses and increased sentencing  for offenders when someone was injured  as a result the charges could be  upgraded against a 22 year old driver  charged with aggravated assault after he  struck and killed nine year old Dale and  Thomas while he was boarding a school  bus on Wednesday we've got to be extra  vigilant when we're in school zones when  we're around school buses because  children don't always have the judgment  to recognize the hazards they're  counting on adults to look out for their  safety and speaking of looking out for  safety school bus stop locations are  often the responsibility of local  authorities or the school districts  themselves were also reminded that as  daylight saving ends this weekend it's  responsible it's the responsibility of  all of us to take extra precautions as  many kids are gonna be going to school  in the dark be honor all of our  responsibilities those videos are so  hard to watch Tony thank you
 

